WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en-GB

00:00:07.359 --> 00:00:08.803
May we then move on?

00:00:08.803 --> 00:00:13.440
We come now to the Committee Report.

00:00:13.440 --> 00:00:19.119
By the way, I should just stress, of course,
that these committees are doing the work of

00:00:19.119 --> 00:00:24.740
the Board; these are outreaches of the Board
with delegated powers, so we take them as

00:00:24.740 --> 00:00:28.130
part of the business of the Board, and I know
that all members of the Board have read the

00:00:28.130 --> 00:00:30.160
reports.

00:00:30.160 --> 00:00:34.930
The consequence of that is there is one report
which is from the Specialised Commissioning

00:00:34.930 --> 00:00:45.110
Committee, that I am just going to invite
Noel, if I may, to say a few words about.

00:00:45.110 --> 00:00:46.530
Thank you, Malcolm.

00:00:46.530 --> 00:00:52.120
As you will know, the Specialised Commissioning
Committee has recently been established to

00:00:52.120 --> 00:00:59.700
bring more coherence to the whole of our Specialised
Commissioning activity, and coherence in three

00:00:59.700 --> 00:01:01.040
particular areas.

00:01:01.040 --> 00:01:09.950
One is our strategy, two is our rolling service
reviews, and three is our investment profile.

00:01:09.950 --> 00:01:15.720
You will see from the more detailed papers
that are available on the website that we

00:01:15.720 --> 00:01:26.070
had our inaugural two sessions on 24th and
30th June, which did indeed deal with our

00:01:26.070 --> 00:01:30.670
investment portfolio for the current year.

00:01:30.670 --> 00:01:38.600
The streamlining of the advice and the process
by which those investment portfolio decisions

00:01:38.600 --> 00:01:47.210
are made was the subject of our teleconference
on the 24th, and that was prior to a meeting

00:01:47.210 --> 00:01:55.860
of the SCOG on 24th June, which then came
forward for the full committee review on the

00:01:55.860 --> 00:01:56.860
30th.

00:01:56.860 --> 00:02:04.820
I am pleased to say that, of the recommendations
that came forward for commissioning new drugs

00:02:04.820 --> 00:02:14.500
this year, of the 26 that were recommended
by our advisory panels there was approval

00:02:14.500 --> 00:02:17.790
throughout.

00:02:17.790 --> 00:02:24.060
There were two particular drugs which we were
unable to decide upon pending NICE review,

00:02:24.060 --> 00:02:31.560
which will be available to us to consider
again later this year and in the spring of

00:02:31.560 --> 00:02:35.790
next year.

00:02:35.790 --> 00:02:42.450
I know there is a huge amount of public interest
and indeed patient interest in the activities

00:02:42.450 --> 00:02:48.890
of the Specialised Commissioning Committee
this particular time round, and you will know

00:02:48.890 --> 00:02:54.730
that we can access all of those papers and
the logic behind the decisioning and the methodology

00:02:54.730 --> 00:03:00.760
that was used, in our public disclosures on
the website.

00:03:00.760 --> 00:03:05.840
Thank you very much, Noel.

00:03:05.840 --> 00:03:10.209
May I invite the Board to approve the terms
of reference for the committee, which are

00:03:10.209 --> 00:03:13.700
set out in the paper before you?

00:03:13.700 --> 00:03:15.140
Thank you very much.

00:03:15.140 --> 00:03:19.670
That brings us to the end of the agenda for
the meeting in public.

00:03:19.670 --> 00:03:25.720
I have only one item of other business, which
is to report the date of our next meeting,

00:03:25.720 --> 00:03:31.739
which will be in London on 24th September
2015.

00:03:31.739 --> 00:03:36.610
At this stage then, I invite the Board to
go into private session, and I declare the

00:03:36.610 --> 00:03:38.800
public meeting of the Board to be closed.

00:03:38.800 --> 00:03:41.000
Thank you very much everybody for attending
this morning.

